---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';

// Add your Buy Me a Coffee or Ko-fi link here when it’s ready.
const coffee = '';
const substack = SITE.links.find((l) => l.label === 'Substack');
---
<Base title="Data" description="Datasets I maintain in my spare time.">
  <h1>Data</h1>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>Alongside the toolbox, I maintain a few datasets in my spare time.</p>

    <div class="dataset">
      <h2>Swedish job market</h2>
      <p>
        Job ads collected by web scraping, then cleaned and labelled by me, so they give an honest
        record of which data jobs actually appear in Sweden and how that changes over time.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="dataset">
      <h2>Simulated population data</h2>
      <p>
        Starting from generalised statistics published by Swedish public services, I’m building a
        simple simulation that estimates fine-grained data from coarse totals. It isn’t finished yet.
      </p>
    </div>

    <p>
      I use these datasets for small hobby projects: deeper analysis and a better understanding of the society I live in.
    </p>

    <p>
      The raw sources are free, but designing, continously scraping, cleaning, labelling and maintaining the data takes time. So the cleaned datasets will be available as paid data products on platforms like AWS Data Exchange. If you find them useful, buying them is the best way to support the work, and it keeps me motivated to keep the data going. My hope is that, a few years from now, this becomes a trustworthy source of data that people rely on.
    </p>

    <p class="muted">Everything here is still a work in progress.</p>

    {substack && (
      <div class="writing">
        <h2>I also write</h2>
        <p>
          In my spare time I also love writing. My blog,
          <a href={substack.href}>stockholm5pm</a> on Substack, is where I write about everything big and small.
        </p>
      </div>
    )}
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  h1 { margin-bottom: 2rem; }
  .prose { max-width: 36rem; }
  .dataset { padding: 1rem 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  .dataset:last-of-type { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
  .dataset h2 { font-size: 1.125rem; margin-bottom: 0.35rem; }
  .dataset p { margin: 0; color: var(--muted); }
  .writing { margin-top: 3rem; padding-top: 1rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  .writing h2 { font-size: 1.125rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
</style>